WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.874 line:0%
Mare is a sergeant detective

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:11.177
<i> living in a community
 in Pennsylvania.</i>

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.045
MARE SHEEHAN: If you got
something you wanna tell me,

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:14.047
you better do it now

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.915
'cause I'm gonna start digging
through your life,

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.283
and I'm gonna find out
everything.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.052
And if you're lying to me, it's
going to be very bad for you.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.023
KATE WINSLET:
<i> There's an unsolved crime
 within the community,</i>

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:25.825
<i> so all eyes have been on Mare</i>

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:29.028
<i> because it's fallen to her,
 and she so far has failed.</i>

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.363
BRAD INGELSBY:<i> The community's
 labeled her a hero,</i>

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.032
<i>but she never felt like a hero.</i>

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.701 line:0%
There's a constant conflict
in Mare

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.203 line:0%
of trying to uphold this image,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.539
<i> even though she knows
 in her heart it's crumbling.</i>

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.307
COLIN ZABEL: I'm just here
to help you find out

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.508
what happened
to those two girls.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.343
Given your relationships
here in town,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.112
it couldn't have been easy
on you.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:47.981
She deals with a lot.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.782
She carries
enormous personal grief.

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:53.086
<i> We do come to understand
 why she is the way she is</i>

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.354
<i> and why she's had to make
 herself that strong</i>

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.256
with that kind of
coarse exterior.

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:58.658
And it's all a coping mechanism.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:02.695
<i> She's just an everyday woman
coping with an enormous amount.</i>

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.099
SPEAKER:
Can I ask if you're seeing
anyone now? Just to talk.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.034
It's been my experience
that it helps parents

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:11.438
-who've lost children-
-No. No, I never... um...

00:01:13.505 --> 00:01:16.609
CRAIG ZOBEL:<i> Mare's journey
on the show involves struggles,</i>

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:20.179
<i> and the fact that she lost
 her son to suicide</i>

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.215 line:0%
and that she has to move on
from that

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.650 line:0%
in order to really grow
and be able to be

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.719
<i> the detective
 that the community needs.</i>

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.189
WINSLET:<i> I loved how vulnerable
 /</i>

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:33.192
<i> and strong at the same time
 Mare truly is.</i>

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.094
She's this extraordinary
dichotomy

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.630
of both of those things,
and that sense of her

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.866
<i> really being entrenched
 in the community.</i>

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.000
(GUNSHOTS)

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.438
<i> I really did find myself
 becoming incredibly immersed</i>

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:49.241
<i> in this character, largely
 because of the fine details</i>

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:52.177
<i> I had to know because
 any sergeant detective</i>

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.247
<i>investigating a community murder</i>

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.982
would've had to know
those things too.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.052
INGELSBY:<i> She's just
 a persistent detective.</i>

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.888
<i> She cares about these people.
 I mean, she doesn't admit it.</i>

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.723
<i> There's a level of emotion
 connected to these girls</i>

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:05.558
<i> that makes it personal,</i>

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.259
and she wants to figure out
what happened.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.796
WINSLET:
<i>We cheer for her along the way,</i>

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.466
and that's what I hope people
can identify with the most

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.769
<i> is that she handles everyone
with a great deal of compassion</i>

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.171
<i> and understanding,
 but at the same time,</i>

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:20.907
<i> she's kind of firm but fair.</i>

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.377
<i> She's just
 so remarkably capable,</i>

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.714
<i>stoic, brave woman who's dealing
 with all the elements</i>

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:31.851
<i> of family life and struggle
 and grief</i>

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.319
<i> and trying to do her best</i>

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:35.654
<i> as a mother,
 as a young grandmother,</i>

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:39.792
and as a woman in a community
that look to her

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.561
so often for answers.

